+// The fused 4-bit Q, K and V projections with each thread's part of A in registers. A thread takes the same
+// weight word of every column, which means it needs the same 32 elements of A for all of them. It holds those
+// for a whole k tile, and adds up a column's word across the k tiles itself, so the workgroup only shares the 32
